.TH LINALG 2
.SH NAME
linalg: dgefa, dgesl, printmat \- dense linear equations, by LU factorisation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "linalg.m";
linalg := load LinAlg LinAlg->PATH;
Matrix, Vector: import linalg;

info := linalg->dgefa(a, lda, n, ipvt);
linalg->dgesl(a, lda, n, ipvt, b, job);
linalg->printmat("k", a, lda, m, n);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I LinAlg
is LINPACK's dense solver: Gaussian elimination with partial pivoting.
.PP
Matrices are stored the way scientific programming in C stores them,
linearised in
.B Fortran
.BR order .
For an
.I m
by
.I n
matrix
.IR A ,
the element in row
.I i
and column
.I j
is
.BI a[i+lda*j]\fR,
with 0-origin indexing throughout, including in the permutation vector.
.I Lda
is the leading dimension, so that a succession of problems of differing
sizes can share one array without copying.
.PP
.B Dgefa
factors
.I a
in place and records the pivots in
.IR ipvt .
It returns 0 if the matrix is nonsingular, and otherwise the index of
the column at which a zero pivot was found \- which is a statement about
the matrix and the only way to discover it.
.PP
.B Dgesl
solves using that factorisation, replacing
.I b
with the answer.
.I Job
0 solves
.IR Ax = b ,
and nonzero solves the transposed system.
Because the factorisation is separate, several right-hand sides cost one
factorisation and a solve each.
.PP
.B Printmat
writes a matrix out under a label, for looking at.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/math/linalg.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR frame (2),
.IR krylov (2),
.IR sparse (2),
.IR math-elem (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B Dgefa
returns nonzero for a singular matrix.
Nothing here raises an exception; a caller that ignores that return and
solves anyway gets arithmetic on infinities.
.SH BUGS
Dense and in one process.
For anything built on a grid, where the matrix is sparse and never
formed,
.IR krylov (2)
over
.IR sparse (2)
is the right tool and this is not.
.PP
There is no condition estimate \- LINPACK's
.B dgeco
is not here \- so a matrix that is nearly singular factors without
complaint and returns an answer with as many correct figures as it has,
which may be none.
.PP
The
.B Matrix
adt is declared and unused: every function takes the array, stride and
sizes separately.
